@nb-corp/nb-im uses the following pinned SDKs. License texts for the direct dependencies and adapted donors are included under LICENSES; transitive dependency licenses remain with their installed packages.

0.3.0 bidirectional adapter batch:
- discord.js@14.27.0 (Apache-2.0) — gateway lifecycle and Discord REST/multipart implementation.
- @slack/web-api@8.2.0 and @slack/socket-mode@3.1.0 (MIT) — official Slack API, Socket Mode and external file-upload sequence.
- matrix-js-sdk@44.0.0 (Apache-2.0) — Matrix authenticated HTTP contracts. No crypto store is initialized; encrypted rooms are not supported by this adapter.
- undici@7.29.1 (MIT) — explicit supported peer for Slack Socket Mode.

Identity/thread/media/setup field mappings adapt OpenClaw (MIT, Copyright 2026 OpenClaw Foundation), and Hermes Agent (MIT, Copyright 2025 Nous Research):
- OpenClaw local checkout 3c9b8602b79b2ae2f3c9a76ac7dfb9579ea8eefc: extensions/{discord,slack,matrix}, docs/channels/{discord,slack,matrix}.md.
- Official current OpenClaw source 068022e6e8df38c35d39cc5dadff40e8f58eac2d, fetched by raw GitHub on 2026-10-24: extensions/slack/{package.json,src/client-delivery.ts}, extensions/matrix/package.json. Current Slack uses the same Web API 8.2.0; current Matrix donor uses SDK 43.0.0, while this package validates 44.0.0 against offline wire fixtures.
- Hermes local checkout 9a6108fdf29b: plugins/platforms/{discord,slack,matrix}/adapter.py and Discord adapter_media.py. Official main bda3a363e9695e3f63fce4a7ca85ba17b5fecb61 was observed through GitHub API; the current Slack adapter header confirms slack-bolt Socket Mode. Full-current Hermes behavior was not inferred from the truncated remote excerpt.

The donor plugin hosts, agent runners, permissions and persistent stores are not imported. The package wraps mature SDK lifecycle and adapts the transport data to nb-im-session/1. Matrix retains a small SDK-backed sync loop so the host admission receipt controls cursor advancement.

Existing adapters:

- @larksuiteoapi/node-sdk@1.76.0 — Feishu/Lark official Node SDK. Long-connection and IM calls go through this SDK. License: MIT (see the package LICENSE).
- ws@8.22.0 — WebSocket client and server used for OneBot v11 forward and reverse sockets. License: MIT (see the package LICENSE).

Telegram and WeChat iLink use the platform HTTPS endpoints through an injectable transport. The iLink field names follow @tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin@2.4.10 (MIT, Tencent), which was read as the vendor contract and is not a runtime dependency. Notification code adapted before 0.2.0 is unchanged. Those mappings derive from Apprise 1.13.1 (BSD-2-Clause, commit 1fe1f703ab6eba7c95113123d7032b9ea32d467c) and Message-Push-Nest / nb-message (Apache-2.0; engigu attribution). No donor server, UI or Python runtime is bundled.

0.2.1 aligns optional getUpdates return codes and direct-chat capability with Tencent/openclaw-weixin at 874637a0dbc24050f72d1385add4fc6170a2d726 (MIT): src/api/types.ts, src/monitor/monitor.ts, src/channel.ts. Feishu thread replies use the pinned SDK's im.message.reply API and the official reply_in_thread contract: https://open.feishu.cn/document/server-docs/im-v1/message/reply.
